      "content": "I'll read the original test and the CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. Let me write a more understandable version with descriptive names, constants, and clarifying comments.Now I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored test replaces cryptic auto-generated variable names (`stringReader0`, `long0`, `int0`) with descriptive names (`sourceContent`, `maxChars`, `charsSkipped`, `readResult`), removes the unused `PipedReader` import, extracts magic numbers into named constants, and adds comments explaining the non-obvious behaviors of `reset()` without a prior mark and the tight read-ahead limit causing an immediate EOF."
